ok reset-foreign: main, a branch and a tag that do not hold the base: `reset` and `reset --yes` exit 2 (`does not hold the recorded base ...; nothing changed`), no plan, the refs unchanged
ok reset-empty: an empty origin: `reset` and `reset --yes` exit 2, `no main on ...: publish the base first`, nothing pushed
ok publish: the plan changes nothing; `--yes` creates someone/own-sandbox (public), pushes the base to main and writes `sandbox.local.json`; a second one, and another name, are refused (exit 2)
ok eval-root: setup refuses a workspace outside the eval root, a missing and a malformed file (exit 2, nothing created); inside, it passes with the allow rules and no trust entry
